Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:49:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 097/202] [ae-patch] Play a token defrag in the composer tray
 while a conversation compacts

Compaction showed only a line of text. While a compaction runs, the tray
above the composer now shows a strip of pills: the system prompt, tools,
memory and skills stay put, and message pills hop left one at a time, dock
at the end of a summary pill and melt into it. When compaction finishes the
pills pour into the context ring, which is held at the old count until they
land and then eases down to the new one. Compaction reports only its start
and finish, so the percent is a time estimate that eases toward 97% and the
last pills wait for the real finish.

Clicking the strip opens a Win98-style "Defragmenting Context C:" window with
a live cluster map, a legend and a completion box. The compaction marker adds
the before and after token counts for a compaction the page watched finish.
Settings > Chat has a switch to turn it off (ae.tokenDefrag, in the settings
export list). Reduced motion takes pills in without the hop.

New files carry the logic (lib/aeTokenDefrag.ts, components/AeTokenDefrag.tsx
and .css); upstream files change by a few lines each: the tray mount in
ChatPage, the ring's held count and pulse, the marker's item id and counts,
the settings export key, and the before count taken in the AE stream tap.
